# The suites of tools/suite.list on Windows (Git Bash of the GitHub runner, Maat 1.6.0): one CI job per group
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml, job windows-gruppo), `tools/suite.sh --gruppi tools/suite-gruppi-windows.list --gruppo k/n`.
# Lines: «<group> [VAR=value …] <entry>» (the entry runs in that group, with those variables) and «- <entry> <reason>»
# (left out on Windows: counted as covered, written as ESCLUSA in riepilogo.txt). Every entry of suite.list in exactly
# one line; groups 1..n (tools/suite.sh refuses otherwise, tools/suite.test.sh checks the link with ci.yml).
# Balanced on the seconds of the first CI of 1.6.0 on the Windows runner (before block C; driver.test.sh measured
# after it at 409-412 s on the runner, 59-85 s on Linux): group 1 ≈ 1150 s, 2 ≈ 1160, 3 ≈ 1170, 4 ≈ 1140, 5 ≈ 1000. The runner is about
# three times faster than the local Windows machine (gates 234 s against 826).
# Locally the same set: bash tools/suite.sh --gruppi tools/suite-gruppi-windows.list <results dir> (from Git Bash).

# left out on Windows
- test-fast            needs rsync and flock: on Windows it runs in WSL, which the runner does not have (locally at release)
- counterproof         needs rsync and flock: on Windows it runs in WSL, which the runner does not have (locally at release)
- vitest-classify      needs rsync and flock: on Windows it runs in WSL, which the runner does not have (locally at release)
- comandi-equivalenza  needs rsync and flock: on Windows it runs in WSL, which the runner does not have (locally at release)
- tools/oracolo.test.sh  about 70 minutes in Git Bash on the local machine; logic that does not depend on the platform: it runs on Linux and macOS

# group 1: run-phase (1047 s)
1 run-phase
1 tools/suite.test.sh
1 phase-usage
1 session-start
1 stop-hook

# group 2: the expected outputs of the public corpus (1009 s)
2 tools/esempi-equiv.test.sh
2 bash-node
2 cycle-report

# group 3: cycle-state (726 s), plan-check (440 s)
3 cycle-state
3 plan-check

# group 4: finalize, gates, messages, ciclo-worktree, maat-doctor
4 finalize
4 gates
4 messages
4 ciclo-worktree
4 maat-doctor

# group 5: the driver and the short ones
5 driver
5 spazi
5 guard
5 test-review-surface
5 maat-paths
5 senza-wsl
5 phase-events
5 context-pack
5 genericita
5 maat-config
5 harness-merge
5 blocks-independent
